#: ../../../search-analytics.rst:2
msgid "Search analytics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../search-analytics.rst:4
msgid ""
"When someone visits your documentation and uses the built-in :doc:`server "
"side search </server-side-search/index>` feature, Read the Docs will collect "
"analytics on their search queries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../search-analytics.rst:7
msgid ""
"These are aggregated into a simple view of the \"Top queries in the past 30 "
"days\". You can also download this data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../search-analytics.rst:11
msgid ""
"This is helpful to optimize your documentation in alignment with your "
"readers' interests. You can discover new trends and expand your "
"documentation to new needs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../search-analytics.rst:15
msgid "Using search analytics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../search-analytics.rst:17
msgid ""
"To see a list of the top queries and an overview from the last month, go to "
"your project's :menuselection:`Settings --> Search analytics`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../search-analytics.rst:20
msgid "Search analytics demo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../search-analytics.rst:25
msgid "How the search analytics page looks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../search-analytics.rst:27
msgid ""
"The list of top queries shows the latest searches ordered by their "
"popularity. Use the :guilabel:`Results` filter to show only queries with or "
"without results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../search-analytics.rst:31
msgid "Understanding your analytics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../search-analytics.rst:33
msgid ""
"In the list of top queries, you can see the most popular terms that users "
"have searched for. Next to the search query, the number of actual "
"**results** for that query is shown. The number of times the query has been "
"used in a search is displayed as the **queries** number."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../search-analytics.rst:37
msgid ""
"If you see a search term that doesn't have any results, you could apply that "
"term in documentation articles or create new ones. This is a great way to "
"understand missing gaps in your documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../search-analytics.rst:41
msgid ""
"If a search term is often used but the documentation article exists, it can "
"also indicate that it's hard to navigate to the article."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../search-analytics.rst:44
msgid ""
"Repeat the search yourself and inspect the results to see if they are "
"relevant. You can add keywords to various pages that you want to show up for "
"searches on that page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../search-analytics.rst:47
msgid ""
"In **Overview**, you can see the daily search totals for the last month, and "
"trends that might match special events in your project's publicity. If you "
"wish to analyze these numbers in details, click :guilabel:`Download search "
"data` to get a CSV formatted file with all available search analytics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../search-analytics.rst:53
msgid "Data storage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../search-analytics.rst:55
msgid ""
"The duration of analytics data stored depends on which site you're using:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../search-analytics.rst:57
msgid "On |org_brand|, the last 90 days are stored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../search-analytics.rst:58
msgid ""
"On |com_brand|, storage duration starts at 30 days and increases with plan "
"level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../search-analytics.rst:62
msgid "`Our plan pricing <https://about.readthedocs.com/pricing/>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../search-analytics.rst:63
msgid "Compare our plan pricing and analytics storage duration."
msgstr ""

